#: ../../source/docs/precision-landing-irlock.rst:66
#: 772fc424b41c48ada78a9782121fce9d
msgid ""
"The IR-LOCK sensor should be mounted to the underside of the frame with "
"the camera lens pointing directly down toward the ground.  A mounting "
"bracket for IRIS is sold `here "
"<https://irlock.com/collections/frontpage/products/sensor-bracket-for-"
"iris>`__ (and pictured below).  The sensor board should be oriented so "
"that the white button on the board points towards the front of the "
"vehicle (or to put it another way, the side closest to the camera lens "
"should be towards the front of the vehicle)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/precision-landing-irlock.rst:75
#: aee953a649844eb88303cb982775688d
msgid ""
"The image below shows the camera mounted on the *bottom* of a 3DR IRIS+. "
"It is probably best to mount the sensor as close as possible to the "
"autopilot, but successful tests have also been performed with various "
"mounting locations."
msgstr ""

